# CODEOWNERS — required reviewers for security-sensitive paths (#0g).
#
# Per docs/ROLES.md the Security Engineer has veto power over internal/crypto,
# internal/auth, and the promotion engine; CLAUDE.md requires review before
# changes that touch crypto, auth, or promotion. CODEOWNERS makes that
# enforceable: a PR touching these paths cannot merge without an owner review
# (pair with branch protection: "Require review from Code Owners" on `main`).
#
# @santapong is the repo-owner placeholder; replace with the security team
# handle/group when one exists.

# --- Cryptography & key management (Type-1; Security veto) ---
/backend/internal/crypto/                       @santapong

# --- Authentication / authorization (Type-1; Security veto) ---
/backend/internal/auth/                         @santapong

# --- Promotion engine (Type-1; Security veto). No single package: the engine
#     spans these files across api/service/repository. ---
/backend/internal/service/promotion_service.go  @santapong
/backend/internal/repository/promotion_repo.go  @santapong
/backend/internal/api/handlers_promotion.go     @santapong
/backend/internal/api/promotion_gate.go         @santapong

# --- CI/CD supply chain. Workflows run with repo credentials; changes here can
#     alter what executes against `main`. ---
/.github/workflows/                             @santapong
/.github/CODEOWNERS                             @santapong
